Input: {"correlation_id": "ETH-USDT-1h-1790002799999", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790040600000, "account": {"equity": "9991.638989133462", "available_margin": "9904.118711133462400000000000", "currency": "USDT", "position_mode": "HEDGE", "as_of_ms": 1790040600000}, "position": {"position_id": "wf-main-5", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "quantity": "0.159", "mark_price": "2752.21", "ownership_role": "MAIN", "as_of_ms": 1790040600000, "entry_price": "2749.714944", "unrealized_pnl": "0.396713904"}, "positions": [{"position_id": "wf-main-5", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "quantity": "0.159", "mark_price": "2752.21", "ownership_role": "MAIN", "as_of_ms": 1790040600000, "entry_price": "2749.714944", "unrealized_pnl": "0.396713904"}], "executor_state": {"as_of_ms": 1790040600000, "controller_id": "brooks-walkforward-10d", "fills_read_status": "available", "executors": [{"executor_id": "wf-exec-9", "status": "RUNNING", "trading_pair": "ETH-USDT", "controller_id": "brooks-walkforward-10d", "position_id": "wf-main-5", "config": {"stop_price": "2718.090000000000000000000000", "target_price": "2812.139999999999999999999999"}}]}, "open_orders": [], "recent_fills": [{"fill_id": "wf-fill-9", "order_id": "wf-fill-9", "position_id": "wf-main-5", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "status": "FILLED", "quantity": "0.159", "price": "2749.714944", "fee": "0.1748818704384", "filled_at_ms": 1790005679999}], "fills_since_last_event": [], "original_trade_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "ENTER_LONG", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790002799999, "market_context": {"regime": "bull-trend", "phase": "breakout-spike with a tight range at the highs", "location": "price holds above the twice-tested H4 2700 zone (H4 bar 108 high 2700, H4 bar 118 high 2700) inside a 21-bar M15 tight range (bar 98 low 2702.56 to bar 119 high 2747.76); first opposing level 2771 (D1 bar-89 spike high), then 2850 (M15 bar 98 / H4 bar 120 high)", "always_in": "long", "notes": "H4 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789991999999) and D1 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789948799999) both read bull-trend/breakout-spike; D1 context is used only for the 2771 spike-high location, and raw closed M15/H1 bars are the entry evidence."}, "setup": {"type": "breakout pullback: buy the breakout of the 21-bar M15 tight range that has held above the broken 2700 H4 double top", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["H1", "M15", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "breakout_pullback", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 119 high (range high)", "price_field": "high", "price": "2747.76", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 119, "open_time_ms": 1790001900000, "close_time_ms": 1790002799999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 117 low (low of the recent higher-low cluster 2718.09/2720.15/2718.23; back into the middle of the tight range)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2718.09", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 117, "open_time_ms": 1790000100000, "close_time_ms": 1790000999999}}, "evidence_for": ["M15 bar 119 (open 2733.06, close 2734.92) is the highest close of the 21-bar consolidation and takes out the prior range highs: 2739.54 (bar 112), 2741.55 (bar 115), 2742.56 (bar 118), then 2747.76 (bar 119) - range highs are rising into the close.", "The M15 range since the spike bar 98 (open 2708.33, high 2850, low 2702.56, close 2739.13) has held entirely above 2702.56, i.e. above the H4 2700 zone that had been tagged twice (H4 bar 108 high 2700, H4 bar 118 high 2700) - a tight consolidation above a broken double top, not a pullback below it.", "H1 follow-through per the H4 transition condition: H1 bars 117-119 (open_time 1789992000000 / 1789995600000 / 1789999200000) closed 2734.09, 2734.13, 2734.92, all above the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15, with lows 2719.08 / 2720.15 / 2718.09 above 2700.", "H1 bar 119 (open 2734.63, high 2747.76, low 2718.09, close 2734.92) makes a higher high versus H1 bar 118 high 2741.55 and closes at the top of the last five H1 bars (lows 2709.56, 2713.04, 2719.08, 2720.15, 2718.09 all hold above 2700).", "M15 lows have stopped falling under the range: 2718.23 (bar 116), 2718.09 (bar 117), 2731.83 (bar 118), 2731.83 (bar 119), so a stop below 2718.09 is a defensible structural invalidation with a defined 29.67-point risk from the 2747.76 trigger."], "evidence_against": ["M15 bar 98 printed 2850 and closed 2739.13, a 147.44-point bar with a 110.87-point upper tail; the whole 21-bar range sits inside that tail, so the buy trigger 2747.76 is still 102.24 below a level that was just rejected.", "H4 bar 120 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) left a 126.85-point upper tail with no follow-through bar in the window; the H4 context flags two earlier upside spikes (bar 61 high 2680, bar 81 high 2609.02) that were fully retraced.", "Overhead structure crowds the setup versus its invalidation: 2747.76 is only 5.20 above the prior M15 range high 2742.56 and only 23.24 below the 2771 D1 spike high, against a 29.67-point stop distance.", "Bar 119 is a weak breakout bar, not a bull trend bar closing on its high: its close 2734.92 sits in the lower ~19% of its 2731.83-2747.76 range with a 12.84 upper tail.", "The 21-bar M15 range is only about 45 points (1.6%) and oscillates around the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15 - consistent with balance at the breakout level, and tight-range breakouts frequently fail without a strong breakout bar."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the M15 tight range resolves upward or becomes a final flag: no bar in the supplied packet closes above 2747.76, so the breakout is untriggered and unconfirmed.", "The would-be signal bar is already printed (bar 119) and is marginal (new high by 5.20 with a 12.84 upper tail); a stronger bull bar closing on its high would raise confidence in the same trigger.", "The D1 context is 15 hours older than the frozen decision time and its 2771/2557 levels are contextual descriptions; the D1 spike high 2771 was exceeded only by a wick (M15 bar 98 high 2850) with no close above it."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A M15 close back below 2731.83 (bar 119 low) and then below 2718.09 (bar 117 low) would mark a failed breakout of the range high and void the long case.", "A M15/H1 close below 2702.56 (bar 98 low) would break the three-hour acceptance above the H4 2700 zone and return price to the prior H4 wide range.", "Repeated M15 closes between 2718.09 and 2747.76 without exceeding 2747.76 would keep the tight-range read and argue against a breakout.", "A M15 close above 2747.76 with the low holding above 2731.83 would confirm the breakout and shift the focus to 2771 and then 2850."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "NO_TRADE", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790038799999, "market_context": {"regime": "bull trend on D1 (breakout-spike) and H4 (channel), but the M15 decision frame is an unresolved tight trading range after a bull spike", "phase": "M15 spike-and-consolidation; H4 possible buy-climax spike (1789977600000 upper tail 126.85); D1 breakout-spike with climax risk", "location": "M15 price 2762.69-2785.48 sits directly under the 2804.59 spike high (M15 1790021700000) and the D1/H4 2850 climax high; it is the lower half of a 23-point tight range whose pullback low 2759.63 (M15 1790020800000) has held", "h1_read": "H1 bar 1790020800000 (open 2760.51, high 2804.59, close 2781.77) is the spike; the last four H1 closes 2781.77, 2768.10, 2775.61, 2762.69 overlap between 2762.69 and 2785.48, and H1 1790035200000 (open 2775.60, low 2762.69, close 2762.69) closes on its low but only marginally under the 2762.93 low of H1 1790024400000", "m15_read": "M15 bars 1790022600000-1790037900000 (18 bars) overlap between 2759.63 and 2785.48 with mid-range closes; the final bar 1790037900000 (open 2770.84, high 2772.69, low 2762.69, close 2762.69) is a bear bar closing at its low, a first downside breakout attempt with no follow-through bar"}, "setup": {"type": "unresolved tight trading range / bull flag under a prior spike high", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "poor", "no_trade_reason": "balanced_context"}, "decision_timeframe": null, "context_timeframes_used": ["H1", "M15", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "unclear", "trigger": null, "invalidation": null, "evidence_for": ["Long-side location is crowded: a stop-entry above the consolidation high 2785.48 (M15 1790031600000, high 2785.48) sits only 19.07 below the 2804.59 spike high (M15 1790021700000, high 2804.59), so the nearest opposing structure is closer than a structural invalidation near the 2762.69 range low (M15 1790037900000, low 2762.69), roughly 25.85 points away.", "The zone above the market already rejected buyers once: M15 1789983000000 (open 2708.33, high 2850, close 2739.13) printed the 2850 high with a ~111-point upper tail and the following M15 bars 1789983900000-1789991100000 closed 2711.92-2723.15, about 130 points below that high.", "The decision bar itself gives no confirmable trigger: M15 1790037900000 (open 2770.84, high 2772.69, low 2762.69, close 2762.69) is a bear bar closing on its low and only a marginal new low of the 18-bar range (prior range low 2762.93 at M15 1790025300000); the pullback low 2759.63 (M15 1790020800000 low) is still intact.", "Context agrees with abstaining on trend-following: both D1 and H4 contexts report breakout-spike/possible buy-climax behavior (D1 final bar high 2850, close 2775.61; H4 1789977600000 close location 33.9% of a 191.94 range with a 126.85 upper tail), so a same-bar long breakout at 2785.48 would be bought into the top of that spike rather than into a fresh edge.", "Short-side room is also crowded: the first support under the range low is 2759.63 (M15 1790020800000 low) only ~3 points away, and the H4 context is always-in long with high relevance, so a stop-sell breakout below 2762.69 is a first breakout of a tight range against the higher-timeframe always-in lean."], "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the higher-timeframe trend is up and intact. D1 has rising closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61 with the last close above the prior 2771 spike high, and H4 shows rising lows 2358.62-2370.54-2438.33-2568.16 with the last three M15/H4 bars holding above the spike bar's midpoint; under that read the 18-bar M15 range is a bull flag, so a stop-entry long above 2785.48 (M15 1790031600000 high) is a standard breakout-pullback continuation and abstaining may miss it.", "Secondary counterargument for the other side: M15 highs descend 2785.48 (1790031600000), 2775.61 (1790034300000), 2776.18 (1790037000000), 2772.69 (1790037900000) while the final bar closes at the range low, so a stop-sell below 2762.69 with invalidation above 2775.61 (M15 1790034300000 high) offers about 13 points risk against roughly 28 points to the 2734.22 low (M15 1790012700000) - a defensible, if counter-trend, measured structure."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the 18-bar M15 range (2759.63-2785.48) is a bull flag that resolves up or a topping flag under the 2804.59/2850 climax; the supplied bars show no confirmed break in either direction at the decision time.", "The H4 and D1 labels (breakout-spike, always-in long, medium confidence) disagree in character with the H4 spike bar's 126.85-point upper tail and 33.9% close location, so context labels and raw bar shape point in opposite directions.", "No bar exists after M15 1790037900000, so the pending state of both potential breakouts is not evidence of failure; the range could still resolve in either direction on the next bar."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A close above 2785.48 (M15 1790031600000 high) with a hold above 2762.69 would resolve the tight range up and make the bull-flag continuation actionable.", "A close below 2759.63 (M15 1790020800000 low) followed by a close below 2734.22 (M15 1790012700000 low) would confirm the downside breakout and shift the M15 read to a lower-high reversal inside the H4 range.", "A close above 2804.59 (M15 1790021700000 high) that holds would mark acceptance above the spike high and weaken the climax reading; a close back below 2713.04/2718.09 would indicate the 2804.59 spike failed.", "H4 resolution: a close below 2658.06 (H4 1789977600000 low) would mark the H4 spike as failed and materially change the bull-trend read."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790035199999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["The window opens at 2109.85 (close of 1779667200000) after a 2139.34 high, then declines 13 bars to 1368.42 (low of 1780704000000), about 36% below 2139.34.", "Bar 1780704000000 has a 230.85 range with a 200.13 lower tail and closes at 1568.55 (top ~13% of its range); bar 1780790400000 (open 1568.55, high 1690.78, low 1563.52, close 1687.83) is a bull reversal bar closing at its high.", "From 1780790400000 to 1787011200000 (73 bars) price overlaps repeatedly between 1512.91 (low of 1782432000000) and 1974.46 (high of 1785110400000); closes cluster 1550-1950 with many overlapping bodies and mixed closes (two-sided range).", "Bar 1787097600000 breaks out: open 1916.51, high 2293.80, low 1905.63, close 2252.16, a 388.17-point bull trend bar closing in the top ~11% of its range and above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bar 1787270400000 spikes to 2771 with a 445.69 range, closing 2515.30 and leaving a ~255.70 upper tail.", "Bars 1787184000000 through 1789603200000 (27 bars) stay between 2357.18 (low of 1788307200000) and 2680 (high of 1789084800000); bodies overlap and closes sit mostly 2380-2530.", "The last four closes are 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61; the final bar (open 2642.90, high 2850, low 2641.70, close 2775.61) closes above the prior spike high 2771 in the upper 64% of its 208.30-point range."], "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument: the largest single directional move in the window is the opening 12-bar, ~36% bear leg to 1368.42, so the bull-trend label rests only on the last ~34 bars, and the 73 bars before that are balance, not trend.", "The 27 bars ahead of the final push are a two-sided range (2357.18-2680) with heavy overlap and mid-range closes; 2850 is a first-bar probe only 79.00 above 2771, and single-bar breakouts of multi-week range tops often fail and re-enter the range.", "Bar 1787270400000 (445.69 range, close 2515.30, ~255.70 upper tail) followed by a 27-bar stall is spike-high behavior consistent with a temporary exhaustion and a market capped by a range boundary rather than a functioning bull channel.", "The 208.30-point final bar after an extended advance could be a buy climax; a large bull bar that is immediately retraced would mark exhaustion rather than breakout acceptance."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1790022600000, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-5"], "reason": "The snapshot is coherent: one MAIN LONG leg (wf-main-5, 0.159) matches the executor mapping (wf-exec-9, position_id wf-main-5) and the single FILLED fill quantity (wf-fill-9, 0.159 at 2749.714944), hedge_state is single_main with unresolved false and hedge_ratio 0, and margin_health is SAFE. management_policy sets strategy_stop_required false, so the empty open_orders list is policy-compliant, and the executor config still carries stop_price 2718.09 (the recorded M15 bar 117 invalidation low) with target 2812.14. The recorded premise (breakout-pullback long above the M15 ran